🟢 5. Correlation and Regression
Covariance vs. Correlation
 are key concepts in statistics for understanding the relationship between two variables
 Covariance measures how two variables change together.
If both increase together → covariance is positive
If one increases while the other decreases → negative
If no consistent pattern → close to zero

Correlation measures both the strength and direction of a linear relationship between two variables. It is the scaled version of covariance.
Values range from −1 to +1
+1: Perfect positive linear relationship
−1: Perfect negative linear relationship
0: No linear relationship

